"The traditional reasoning follows a specific sequence: a body that has just been sweating in the heat has its pores open, in a state traditionally described as more vulnerable to invasion precisely because the usual protective barrier is relaxed. Stepping directly into strongly air-conditioned air at that moment is traditionally read as inviting cold to enter through those open pores far more easily than it would through a body that had time to cool down gradually and close them again first.": "ea33cd98c92d",
